source_proof = "The pytest gate parses the actual JSON manifests, hashes all 76 registered SQL files, validates the application DAG and monorepo-relative source paths, checks preserved provenance digests and exact unresolved/drifted input inventories, reopens the actual manifests after closing every handle, and checks the real Go producer/consumer admission and history guards as source facts. It parses grants.json to bind required runtime role migrations and checks the real bootstrap path reader and least-privilege readiness test source."
review_only = "No Go/PostgreSQL toolchain is run. Closing and reopening manifest handles proves persisted manifest state only, not a coordinator process restart. Actual legacy catalog fingerprints, import/refusal against mismatched histories, coordinator restart recovery, combined PostgreSQL qualification, deployment reader versions, measured locks, extension version and least-privilege runtime execution remain unproven and required through owner wiring requests. No shell script, unit or build file is changed, so bash -n and native build checks do not apply."
